WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:12.570
Hi! Why are windows made of glass, and raincoats made of plastic? Today let's review materials from Primary 3: their properties, and how we choose them.

2
00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:19.170
The things around us are made of different materials, such as wood, metal, plastic and glass.

3
00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:32.586
There are also rubber, ceramic and fabric. One object can be made of several materials. An umbrella may have a waterproof fabric cover, a metal frame and a plastic handle.

4
00:00:32.736 --> 00:00:37.218
Strength is how much force a material can take without breaking.

5
00:00:37.368 --> 00:00:42.954
A flexible material can bend without breaking, like rubber or a plastic ruler.

6
00:00:43.104 --> 00:00:50.706
To compare hardness, scratch two materials against each other. The one that leaves a scratch on the other is harder.

7
00:00:50.856 --> 00:01:01.362
A waterproof material doesn't let water through. A transparent material lets light through. Some materials float in water, and some sink.

8
00:01:01.512 --> 00:01:05.634
Glass is transparent, so a glass window lets light in.

9
00:01:05.784 --> 00:01:11.178
Rubber is flexible and waterproof, so it is good for tyres and rain boots.

10
00:01:11.328 --> 00:01:16.194
Metal is strong and lets heat through quickly, so pots are made of metal.

11
00:01:16.344 --> 00:01:22.842
Plastic is waterproof and light, so raincoats are often made of plastic.

12
00:01:22.992 --> 00:01:27.642
Watch out! Hardness and strength are not the same property!

13
00:01:27.792 --> 00:01:35.106
Glass is very hard and can scratch many materials, but it shatters if you drop it, so it is not very strong.

14
00:01:35.256 --> 00:01:42.954
We test hardness by scratching, and strength by how much load a material can take before it breaks.

15
00:01:43.104 --> 00:01:54.858
Your turn! Material A leaves a scratch on B, but B cannot scratch A. Which one is harder? Pause and think.

16
00:01:55.008 --> 00:02:03.234
A is harder. The material that scratches the other one is the harder one. Did you get it right?

17
00:02:03.384 --> 00:02:13.506
Another one! The cover of an umbrella must be made of a material with which property? Pause and think.

18
00:02:13.656 --> 00:02:20.034
It must be waterproof, so the rain can't get through. Did you get it right?

19
00:02:20.184 --> 00:02:31.434
Next one! A wooden block and an iron nail are put in water. Which floats, and which sinks? Pause and think.

20
00:02:31.584 --> 00:02:40.410
The wooden block floats and the iron nail sinks. That is why rafts are often made of wood. Did you get it right?

21
00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:49.458
Last one! Why are buckets usually not made of glass? Pause and think.

22
00:02:49.608 --> 00:02:59.466
Because glass breaks easily. A bucket gets carried and knocked about, so plastic or metal is stronger. Did you get it right?

23
00:02:59.616 --> 00:03:12.642
Remember: materials differ in strength, flexibility, hardness, how waterproof and transparent they are, and whether they float. We choose a material for an object by the properties it needs.

24
00:03:12.792 --> 00:03:18.570
Find something at home and think about why it is made of that material!

